{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/269548-shift-concequence","id":269548,"title":"Shift Concequence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-30T15:38:26-07:00","id":269548,"title":"Shift Concequence","content":"In <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/269417-does-this-sound-unreasonable-to-you\">this thread</a> the wise PenDragon mentioned Shift Consequence and it being very overpowered. I did not want to hijack the thread, but did want to ask about that. I have currently one PC who has that power in Night Train, and wanted to ask if it has proven disruptive, is mostly just a potentially disruptive thing, or if people have made house rules to limit it without completely nerfing it. The PC in question is built such that she can often pass cover checks (though this turned out to be retroactively true rather than a building intention) if that is a factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T15:44:37-07:00","id":269568,"title":"","content":"I've had a demon PC for a few months now who started with Shift Consequence and has not actually used it once to date. That's partially because of her poor activation pool, but still, this is a power where Your Mileage May Vary, especially with regards to what kind of consequences your PC is typically in range of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T15:47:03-07:00","id":269572,"title":"","content":"I converted it into a Exploit, because it is far more exploitish (gross manipulation of Time and Causality) than it is an Embed. Then replaced it with this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:19px\">Close Call</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">By nudging probability a Demon can eek by misfortune through the power of sheer circumstance. The bullet aimed at him collides with the smartphone in his shirt pocket, he bends over to pick up a coin right when a searcher would pick him out in a crowd, he gets sand in his eyes just as the Ventrue attempts to mesmerize him. This embed must be activated the instant misfortune befalls him (or the victim, if he is using this on behalf of another) and the protection must be </span>plausible<span style=\"font-size:15px\"> as simple circumstance. If the event cannot plausibly be avoided, such as a collapsing skyscraper </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">not </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">crushing the man in the lobby, this embed will have no effect.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: Wits + Streetwise</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><u>Roll Results</u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure: The very act he attempted to prevent instead succeeds with flying colors. The enemy gains an exceptional success, even if his roll would have been a failure.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure: No effect; events playout unchanged.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success: The misfortune is diverted in the most minimal, plausible manner possible. The Demon has no control over how the misfortune is avoided, nor can he judge any other consequences that may arise from the failure. If there was a roll involved, it automatically fails. Supernatural powers may instead enter a Clash of Wills, at the storyteller's discretion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success: As above, but rolls fail dramatically, in a manner that most benefits the subject of the embed.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>It has roughly similar effects while being more in line with the power of other Embeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-30-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T00:14:02-07:00","id":269896,"title":"","content":"It's in many ways an exploit, but I believe the reason it was kept as an embed is that when you go loud, you know *all* exploits. This way, Shift Consequence is not a 'universal' thing.<br /> <br /> Power-wise, it is very powerful, but also a bit risky. It IS a resisted embed, which can be rather difficult to pull off especially early on, and it's certainly no worse than &quot;kill everyone in the room right now&quot;, &quot;120mm cannons deal 1 damage to their target if I so will it&quot; or &quot;Your next words are whatever I damn well want your words to be and you don't even know it&quot;. Nor is it worse than the words &quot;1+ dots in Celerity&quot;, &quot;Prime 5&quot;, &quot;Mind 5&quot;, or any number of other things in the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Embeds and Exploits don't grow; they're exactly as they are. But their scary abusive practices are flat out explained and pointed out in the descriptive text! A lot of it reads to me like the developers (for once in an RPG) not only understood the mechanics they were working with, but refused to go into denial about all the ways the abilities will be abused, since they were making a game about reality-hacking robots that are supposed to think this way and are piloting giant humans anyways. I mean just think about the common meanings of the word &quot;exploit&quot; when it comes to gaming or network security!<br /> <br /> A mage player has to figure out how to make his new dots into something horrifyingly unexpected, but once he does he can do far more, as might a tremere. A Sin Eater sounds like he'll just do some silly haunting of an area until you realize how insane those manifestations get eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3948,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","user":"Robotboxes","date":". 10-01-2014, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3948-robotboxes","name":"Robotboxes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T00:18:58-07:00","id":269898,"title":"","content":"I'll play devil's advocate (har har).<br /> <br /> I think Shift Consequence is in tone with Embeds. Is it a <i>potent </i>Embed? Yes. Has it the potential to be abused? Hell yes. But, I think that assumes bad faith on the part of the player. If a player picks this Embed and spams it, then her Demon is going to suffer some consequences (ironically enough). Such gross manipulation of reality is gonna call down Angels, even if the character's Cover stays intact. I think there's an <i>implicit </i>limitation to the power, i.e., the setting of the game is one where you have to watch your back at every turn, and screwing with the building bricks of time and causality should be a risk. The Demon isn't the player. She doesn't know that statistically her Manipulation + Wits is a good pool. She might know she's good at preserving her identities, but she isn't going to look at it so black and white (unless she does, which is an interesting character trait...). She knows that that God-Machine is everywhere, and doesn't overlook anything.<br /> <br /> I'm not suggesting that using this power should punish the character, but it should be risky. Yes, you get to put off certain consequences for now, but there may be some later, especially if the power is a crutch for the character.<br /> <br /> Basically, an ST has to be prepared. Shift Consequences can change things up for the plot, but I don't think it's as bulletproof as it's been made out to be. In my personal experience, it was never disruptive. It created some cool story branches, and the player who had it used it to solve puzzles in creative ways. I never felt as though he hid behind it.<br /> <br /> If you trust your player to act in good faith, I don't see a problem. Overpowered is a nebulous thing. Compared to other Embeds? Maybe. But if it's an Exploit, it's actually potentially easier to get past the Compromise. Spend a Willpower; no Compromise.<br /> <br /> &lt;/devil advocating&gt;<br /> <br /> I totally can see how this power would be disruptive, but I think that really comes down to being on the same page as your players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-01-2014, 03:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T01:07:40-07:00","id":269954,"title":"","content":"In general, I trust my players to act in good faith. My worry is not &quot;could a cleaver player abuse this&quot; but more &quot;would a sensible player with it unbalance things by acting sensibly.&quot; Given my group, I don't care (for purposes of the game I am running) if a power can be twisted into being something unbalancing. I'm looking for if normal intelligent use could be an issue, and if so how to fix that.<br /> <br /> I could have been clearer on that, apologies.<br /> <br /> And yea, I am aware of how scary Boneyard can be. ^_^<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T01:28:10-07:00","id":269966,"title":"","content":"Please note, in the thread this question was coming from the OP was explicitly talking about an Angelic sort of antagonist, who would not suffer then Cover breaking effects of Shift Consequence. I called it out there as being potentially problematic for this reason.<br /> <br /> That said, as Yossarian stated, Shift Consequence is certainly not going to be a problem in the hands of a 'cooperative' player. Of course, few things will be a problem in the hands of cooperative players, Exalted 2nd EDs notoriously clunky combat system isn't a problem in the hands of cooperative players. If players are cooperative enough one can eschew dice rolls entirely (as I have in the past).<br /> <br /> That said, it can also be game crushingly disruptive in the wrong hands. So, my advice is as others. If you trust the players, all of them, not to abuse their power then it probably won't be an issue. If you are concerned they might, for some reason (be it malice, panic, misunderstanding or just plain goofiness), get carried away and make changes you aren't really comfortable with managing, be wary.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ninja'd by Baron. In that case, ask yourself, will you be presenting consequences worse than risking cover? How often? And how do you feel about them being redirected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 10-01-2014, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T01:44:32-07:00","id":269969,"title":"","content":"There's also the catch-all that applies to every single Embed: repeated or obviously supernatural exploitation of them results in cover checks. I don't care who you are, the near-omnipotent God-Computer is going to notice that causality constantly doesn't work when Joe Bubbins the Demon is around and shred his Cover to pieces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T08:00:33-07:00","id":270123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/269548-shift-concequence?p=269954#post269954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I trust my players to act in good faith. My worry is not &quot;could a cleaver player abuse this&quot; but more &quot;would a sensible player with it unbalance things by acting sensibly.&quot; Given my group, I don't care (for purposes of the game I am running) if a power can be twisted into being something unbalancing. I'm looking for if normal intelligent use could be an issue, and if so how to fix that.<br /> <br /> I could have been clearer on that, apologies.<br /> <br /> And yea, I am aware of how scary Boneyard can be. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I totally assumed your player would act in good faith, I just wanted to illustrate my point to a general audience -- Shift Consequences threads are a bit frequent. <i>I</i> ought to have been clearer<i>.</i> If it's a matter of it being a power that would be disruptive even <i>with </i>a good player, I don't think you have anything to worry about. It's pretty all-purpose, but if every solution is a hammer, etc.<br /> <br /> And I <i>love </i>how scary Boneyard is! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> However, I completely agree with you, PenDragon. As an antagonist power, it might be too much to lay on characters. I can see it being okay if you're delicate about it, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-01-2014, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T13:14:03-07:00","id":273175,"title":"","content":"Worth pointing out that some Embeds seem to be not so much angel tricks as principles that the Machine uses in general - the Woolworth Infrastructure from Long Road to Canaan is a fairly direct Shift Consequence equivalent, for instance, and, as with that, an angelic application of the power would likely use a specific instance or type of scapegoat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}